cross_domain_transfer.pattern:
Query before dispatch. When the side-effecting call reports success whatever happens (SHOpenFolderAndSelectItems returns S_OK with nothing selected), ask the target system's own filter, through its own documented API, whether the action will do what the user expects. Dispatch only if it will; otherwise say why and do nothing.

The known failure mode is drift between query and dispatcher: the query says yes and the dispatch still does nothing. It is guarded three ways:
- the query is the shell's own state;
- the window cases check against an independent oracle (the registry);
- every cell where query and dispatcher could disagree, and that predicts a landing, is filed for a person to measure.
